st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.

Local desktop setup
-------------------
The [repository installer](../installer/README.md) builds ST, deploys its
source and binary to ~/.config/st, links st into ~/.local/bin, and installs
its terminfo in ~/.terminfo. Press Super + Enter in DWM to open it.

Edit ~/.config/st/config.h to change the font, colors, or shortcuts, then run:

    make -C ~/.config/st

Open a new terminal to use the rebuilt binary. The configured font is
JetBrainsMono Nerd Font. Shift + Up / Down scrolls terminal history one page at a time.
The external scroll helper is built by the installer but is disabled in ST's
default configuration; this fork provides its own scrollback.

The standalone installation instructions below are an upstream reference.
They install to /usr/local instead of updating the installer-managed binary.


Requirements
------------
This build requires a C compiler, Make, pkg-config, and development headers
and libraries for Xlib, Xft, Fontconfig, and FreeType. The tic utility from
ncurses compiles its terminfo.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
For a standalone build without make clean install or the repository installer,
compile the st terminfo entry from the ST source directory:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

